 {"id":"fabro-05d0","title":"Bake gh into the develop toolchain image (or check open PRs engine-side) so the in-flight-PR guard functions","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:40:40.695Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:06:39.364Z","description":"In run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE the planner's mandated gh pr list --state open failed with exit 127 (gh: command not found) and degraded fail-open, so the double-pick guard from fabro-d0c7 (which exists because fabro-22e4 re-implemented a fix waiting in PR #47) is structurally disabled on fabro-toolchain:noble even though the engine has GitHub access (PR #51 was created). Change: add the gh binary to the toolchain image built from .fabro/Dockerfile, or move the open-PR check engine-side using run PR metadata instead of a sandbox binary. Expected effect: the guard actually audits double-picks and one guaranteed erroring tool call disappears from every planning pass.\nBasis: run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE, workflow version ae2869aca84cea61832e77a2926b97ebb79d70300014555c724f2862e12612c9, commit 774f67e9548357656f837bd152c22be72920eb1e","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-07T21:06:39.364Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-5b0a","title":"Surface degraded fail-open planner checks as run-level warnings in the run summary and PR body","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:40:43.171Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:56:07.608Z","description":"In run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE the gh open-PR check degraded fail-open but the degradation was visible only in a journal line; a human reading PR #51 cannot distinguish 'succeeded' from 'succeeded with guards down'. Change: engine-side, emit a run-level warning (surfaced in the run summary and the PR body) whenever a mandated planner check degrades fail-open instead of logging it only to the journal. Expected effect: guard-down runs become human-visible at review time instead of silently passing.\nBasis: run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE, workflow version ae2869aca84cea61832e77a2926b97ebb79d70300014555c724f2862e12612c9, commit 774f67e9548357656f837bd152c22be72920eb1e","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-6f6e","title":"Closeout: warn when the run diff touches a Dockerfile — the fix is inert until the toolchain image rebuilds","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:13:09.464Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:32:11.484Z","description":"Run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ (seed fabro-05d0) delivered only a .fabro/Dockerfile.toolchain edit; Docker is absent from run sandboxes so no build ran and the reviewer approved anyway — the same gap that left gh in .fabro/Dockerfile since commit 98ed9f1 while run containers still hit exit 127 on Sep 7. Change: in .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/closeout.nu, detect a diff touching Dockerfile* and emit a run-level warning ('seed closes, but takes effect only after fabro-toolchain:noble rebuild') surfaced in the run summary and PR body (the channel open seed fabro-5b0a proposes — complementary, cross-referenced, not superseded). Expected effect: eliminates the recurring class of seeds closed green while the promised behavior stays broken for N subsequent runs.\\nBasis: run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 54612515b569d36aa68872cb119b12ae7f9c4eaf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-c0a8","title":"Develop planner: record stale-spec corrections via sd update before claiming","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:13:15.362Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:02:41.168Z","description":"Seed fabro-05d0 named .fabro/Dockerfile as the fix target; the planner burned ~6 tool calls / ~45 s / $0.097 (39% of run cost, events seq 44-82) proving the path wrong, then the implementer re-hit the contradiction and journaled a suggested sd update that nobody applied — the seed closed with the stale body. Change: .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 3 (stale-basis check): when the basis resolves but the spec's named path is wrong, the planner (already the sole tracker writer) must record the correction via sd update <id> --description before claiming. Expected effect: ~40% planner time/token cut on platform-path seeds (the tracker's most common class) and the contradiction stops recurring in every future reader's context.\\nBasis: run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 54612515b569d36aa68872cb119b12ae7f9c4eaf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
+{"id":"fabro-c0a8","title":"Develop planner: record stale-spec corrections via sd update before claiming","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:13:15.362Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T22:04:39.352Z","description":"Seed fabro-05d0 named .fabro/Dockerfile as the fix target; the planner burned ~6 tool calls / ~45 s / $0.097 (39% of run cost, events seq 44-82) proving the path wrong, then the implementer re-hit the contradiction and journaled a suggested sd update that nobody applied — the seed closed with the stale body. Change: .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 3 (stale-basis check): when the basis resolves but the spec's named path is wrong, the planner (already the sole tracker writer) must record the correction via sd update <id> --description before claiming. Expected effect: ~40% planner time/token cut on platform-path seeds (the tracker's most common class) and the contradiction stops recurring in every future reader's context.\\nBasis: run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 54612515b569d36aa68872cb119b12ae7f9c4eaf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-07T22:04:39.352Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-96bd","title":"Implementer prompt: document the ml record flag contract per record type","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:13:20.579Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:32:11.677Z","description":"The implementer's lesson-capture call failed with 'pattern records are missing required flag(s): --name' yet exited 0 with is_error: false (events seq 163-165) — only the stdout text revealed the failure. .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 6 teaches the exact failing form (ml record <domain> --type ... --description ... with no --name). Change: document the exact flag set per record type (pattern requires --name) in step 6, and note the mulch-cli exit-0-on-error bug (same class as sd's fabro-d936) for upstream filing. Expected effect: one fewer failed tool call + LLM round per lesson capture and deterministic error detection.\\nBasis: run 01M1YTVK73YEJXW4542MWDX4BJ, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 54612515b569d36aa68872cb119b12ae7f9c4eaf","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-9a43","title":"Point reviewer phrase checks at read_file offset/limit when diff line numbers are known","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T21:40:22.698Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:49:26.064Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md (tool-guidance/verification section), instruct the reviewer to verify phrase-presence claims with read_file offset/limit on the exact lines the diff already names — or pass an explicit max_results to grep — instead of multi-pattern grep alternations. Grounded in run 01M1YWHK6F8F2VZ6F6FZV8A7VE: the reviewer's first grep alternation returned only the line-25 match in truncated output (journal event seq 174, observation 2), forcing a second targeted grep for the carve-out clause — an extra model round-trip (~3–4 s of the reviewer's 23.7 s) for a verification the diff had already localized to lines 25 and 78. Expected effect: one fewer verification round-trip per review of text-edit seeds. Related to open fabro-a0fe (blob reads with read_file offset/limit) but targets the phrase-check guidance — different section, different mechanism (grep-truncation avoidance vs improvised blob reads).\nBasis: run 01M1YWHK6F8F2VZ6F6FZV8A7VE, workflow version 5603b5e729f24c8e4ab21d9e7599599d18c4c910b381de3682f7a9a6b8628a21, commit 50367ecee388a4806948c80162dc93c2f95f7bb2","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
